# Vite client env - only variables prefixed with VITE_ are exposed to the browser.
#
# Development: copy to `.env` or `.env.local` for overrides. Prefer `.env.local`.
# If unset in dev, the app defaults to http://localhost:8700 (see `src/config/env.ts`).
#
# Production builds: use `.env.production` - copy from `.env.production.example`
# so `vite build` / deploy inlines the deployed worker-api URL. That file is not
# loaded during `vite dev`, so local dev stays on localhost unless you override
# here.
#
# VITE_API_BASE_URL=https://worker-api.example.com
#
# Sentry DSN of the front-app React project. Public by design (inlined into the
# bundle). Unset disables Sentry, which is the usual choice in local dev.
# VITE_SENTRY_DSN=
#
# Sentry `environment` tag, an AppEnvironment value (dev | staging | preview |
# production). Unset: `dev` under `vite dev`, `production` for builds. CD and
# the preview deploy set it.
# VITE_APP_ENVIRONMENT=dev
